  "description": "Five<em> surimono</em> 刷物, privately commissioned prints known literally as \"printed things,\" make up this image of women collecting sea life at low tide. Ten poems written by members of a poetry salon appear across the upper part of the composition. All but one contain the words \"low tide,\" with the remaining poem describing abalone as a sought-after jewel.",
